Getting Started (Web App)
Prerequisites
Node.js 20+
pnpm 9+
PostgreSQL database
1. Install dependencies
pnpm install

2. Set environment variables
Create a .env file or export these variables:

DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/cafe_pos
SESSION_SECRET=your_secret_here

3. Push the database schema
pnpm --filter @workspace/db run push

4. Regenerate API types (optional — already committed)
pnpm --filter @workspace/api-spec run codegen

5. Run the API server
pnpm --filter @workspace/api-server run dev

The API will be available at http://localhost:8080/api

6. Run the frontend
pnpm --filter @workspace/cafe-pos run dev

Open http://localhost:5173 in your browser.

Getting Started (Java Console App)
No dependencies required — just a JDK.

cd cafe-pos
javac CafePOS.java
java CafePOS

Follow the prompts to select an item and quantity. A formatted receipt with subtotal, 5% tax, and grand total is printed to the terminal.

API Endpoints
Method	Endpoint	Description
GET	/api/healthz	Health check
POST	/api/orders	Create and save a new order
GET	/api/orders/:id	Get a single order by ID
GET	/api/orders/daily	Get all orders for a date (?date=YYYY-MM-DD)
GET	/api/orders/monthly	Get orders for a month (?year=&month=)
Example — Create Order
curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "items": [
      { "name": "Latte", "price": 3.50, "quantity": 2 },
      { "name": "Muffin", "price": 3.00, "quantity": 1 }
    ],
    "subtotal": 10.00,
    "tax": 0.50,
    "total": 10.50
  }'

Example — Daily Report
curl "http://localhost:8080/api/orders/daily?date=2025-05-15"

Example — Monthly Report
curl "http://localhost:8080/api/orders/monthly?year=2025&month=5"

Scripts
Command	Description
pnpm --filter @workspace/api-server run dev	Start the API server (dev mode)
pnpm --filter @workspace/cafe-pos run dev	Start the frontend (dev mode)
pnpm --filter @workspace/db run push	Push DB schema changes
pnpm --filter @workspace/api-spec run codegen	Regenerate hooks and Zod schemas
pnpm run typecheck	Full TypeScript check
pnpm run build	Build all packages
Printing Receipts
After placing an order, click Print Receipt in the order confirmation dialog. The browser print dialog will open showing only the receipt — all other UI is hidden via @media print CSS.

